# Playwright rules (sync API only)
- pytest-playwright, sync API; UI tests are plain `def`, not `async def`. Test data via sync httpx / API adapters, never via clicks.
- One browser per worker, new context per test. Set browser_context_args, base_url, storage_state (from the per-run token file: API login once per run under FileLock; only login tests skip it).
- Artefacts: --tracing retain-on-failure --screenshot only-on-failure --video off. Max --reruns 1 in CI, always reported.
- Page Object: locators in __init__ (role/label/test-id first, CSS last), one method per user action, web-first assertions (expect(...)) inside expect_* methods. Component Objects for repeated widgets (TaskCard, KanbanColumn).
- Tests read as business flows (board.create_task(...), board.move_task(task, to=Column.IN_PROGRESS)). No locators, URLs, sleeps or wait_for_timeout in tests.
- Frontend lacks accessible names/test ids: list them in testing/KNOWN_ISSUES.md, use the most stable selector. Adding data-testid to the frontend only under testing-modify-prod.mdc.
- Fast PR subset = @pytest.mark.critical (marker smoke belongs to tests/smoke/). Browser synthetic checks: tests/synthetic/browser/ (marker synthetic), run rarely, policy in cat-smoke-synthetic.md.
- Drag-and-drop (dnd-kit): one helper in the board page object: mouse.move to source, mouse.down, mouse.move(..., steps=N) to target, mouse.up; never drag_to.
